      "role": "user",
      "content": "it says: \"4.2: The Supplier reserves the right to implement fuel surcharges during peak demand periods to accommodate market volatility. These surcharges may be applied via notice to the Client and will take effect 7 days after notification, without requirement for prior written authorization from the Client.\"\n\nthat sounds like they can just notify us and then the price changes, right? if that's the case, then we don't actually have a say in it. is that really as bad as it sounds? i'm just trying to see if this is a dealbreaker or not.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
